allowed.)
(8, 128, 2)
(9, 243, 3)', NULL, '{"a": "(7, 343, 7)", "b": "(10, 500, 4)", "c": "(6, 216, 3)", "d": "(11, 331, 5)"}'::jsonb, NULL, 'a',
  'Pattern: Second number = First number × (Third number)³, or b = a × c³ (alternatively b = a² × c for c=a, but universally b = a × 2⁴ = 128 when c=2, b = a × 3³ = 243 when c=3; notice c=2 gives 2⁴=16, c=3 gives 3³=27; or b = a² × c: 8² × 2 = 128, 9² × 3 = 243).
- Set 1: (8, 128, 2) -> 8² × 2 = 64 × 2 = 128.
- Set 2: (9, 243, 3) -> 9² × 3 = 81 × 3 = 243.
Applying this to options:
- Option (A): (7, 343, 7) -> 7² × 7 = 49 × 7 = 343.
Hence, option (A) follows the exact same logic.', NULL, false, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'verified'
)
