- (D) DG - FI: D(4) + 2 = F(6), G(7) + 2 = I(9) [Shift: +2]
All pairs except FI - JM have a uniform shift of +2 between corresponding letters, whereas FI - JM has a shift of +4.
Hence, option (A) is the odd one out.', NULL, false, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'verified'
)
