2. ''P has the exam on Wednesday'' -> Wednesday = P.
3. ''Only three people have exams after R'' -> Thursday = R.
4. ''S has the exam after Q but before P'' -> Q < S < P(Wed). Thus Monday = Q, Tuesday = S.
5. Available days: Fri(5), Sat(6), Sun(7) for T, U, V.
6. ''U has the exam before V but not on Friday'' -> U cannot be Fri, so Saturday = U, Sunday = V. That leaves Friday = T.
7. Complete schedule: Mon = Q, Tue = S, Wed = P, Thu = R, Fri = T, Sat = U, Sun = V.
8. Number of people between T (Friday) and Q (Monday) = Tue, Wed, Thu = 3 people (S, P, R).
Hence, the correct option is B (Three).', NULL, false, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'verified'
)
