  'Each of P, Q, R, S, T, U and V has an exam on a different day of a week starting from Monday and ending on Sunday of the same week. V has an exam on Thursday. T has an exam on one of the days after P and on one of the days before U. Q has an exam on one of the days after R but on one of the days before S. R has an exam on one of the days after V. Who has an exam on Sunday?', NULL, '{"a": "P", "b": "R", "c": "S", "d": "V"}'::jsonb, NULL, 'c',
  'Step-by-step deduction:
1. Days: Mon(1), Tue(2), Wed(3), Thu(4), Fri(5), Sat(6), Sun(7).
2. ''V has an exam on Thursday'' -> Thursday = V.
3. ''R has an exam on one of the days after V'' -> R is on Fri, Sat, or Sun.
4. ''Q has an exam on one of the days after R but on one of the days before S'' -> R < Q < S.
 Since R is after Thursday, R must be Friday, Q must be Saturday, and S must be Sunday!
5. ''T has an exam on one of the days after P and on one of the days before U'' -> P < T < U on Mon, Tue, Wed.
6. Who has an exam on Sunday? S.
Hence, the correct option is C (S).', NULL, false, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'verified'
)
