  id, master_id, subject, chapter_id, chapter_num, chapter_name, chapter_q_num,
  subtopic, exam_name, exam_tag, exam_stage, exam_date, exam_shift, target_level,
  question_text, question_text_hi, options, options_hi, correct_option,
  solution_text, solution_text_hi, has_image, image_type, svg_content, option_svgs, solution_svg, verification_status
) VALUES (
  'RRB_NTPC_REASON_CH10_Q0040', 2854, 'General Intelligence and Reasoning', 'reason_ch10', 10, 'Puzzle Test', 40,
  'Floor Puzzle', 'RRB NTPC', 'RRB NTPC Graduate Level', 'Stage-I / Stage-II', '24/03/2026', '12:45 PM - 2:15 PM', 'Graduate',
  'J, K, L, R, S and T live on six different floors of the same building. The lowermost floor in the building is numbered 1, the floor above it is numbered 2 and so on till the topmost floor is numbered 6. Only three people live between R and S, where R lives below S. J lives on an odd numbered floor and immediately above R. L lives on one of the floors below K and on one of the floors above T. Who lives on floor number 4?', NULL, '{"a": "T", "b": "R", "c": "L", "d": "J"}'::jsonb, NULL, 'c',
  'Step-by-step deduction:
1. 6 floors: 1 to 6.
2. ''Only three people live between R and S, where R lives below S'' -> |S - R| = 4, so (R=1, S=5) or (R=2, S=6).
3. ''J lives on an odd numbered floor and immediately above R'' (J = R + 1, J is odd):
 - If R = 1: J = 2 (even, contradiction).
 - If R = 2: J = 3 (odd! valid!). Then S = 6.
4. Available floors: 1, 4, 5 for L, K, T.
5. ''L lives on one of the floors below K and on one of the floors above T'' -> T < L < K. Thus T = 1, L = 4, K = 5.
6. Floor arrangement: Floor 6 = S, Floor 5 = K, Floor 4 = L, Floor 3 = J, Floor 2 = R, Floor 1 = T.
7. Who lives on floor number 4? L.
Hence, the correct option is C (L).', NULL, false, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'verified'
)
