  'Read the given statements and conclusions carefully. You have to take the given statements to be true even if they seem to be at variance from commonly known facts. You have to decide which conclusion/s logically follow/s from the given statements. Statements: All vultures are sparrows. Some sparrows are crows. No crow is a pigeon. Conclusions: (I) Some vultures are crows. (II) No sparrow is a pigeon.', NULL, '{"a": "Only conclusion II follows.", "b": "Only conclusion I follows.", "c": "Neither conclusion I nor II follows.", "d": "Both conclusions I and II follow."}'::jsonb, NULL, 'c',
  'Step-by-step syllogism analysis:
Statements: All vultures are sparrows. Some sparrows are crows. No crow is a pigeon.
