al-align:middle; background:#ffffff;\">\n  <rect width=\"180\" height=\"75\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"24\" y=\"44\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#475569\">(D)</text>\n  <text x=\"70\" y=\"44\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1e293b\">Star</text>\n</svg>"}'::jsonb, NULL, 'a',
  'From Dice (2) and Dice (3)â€”
Hence, rectangle will appear on the opposite side of the
triangle.
