  <rect width=\"180\" height=\"75\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"24\" y=\"44\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#475569\">(D)</text>\n  <text x=\"70\" y=\"44\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1e293b\">C</text>\n</svg>"}'::jsonb, NULL, 'a',
  'In figure I and figure 4
Figure (l) Figure (4)
If two faces of dice are in common or equal, then the
third face is opposite to each other.
Hence, opposite face of F is C.
